lesson as a document you can print, then Practice on paper with answers at the back.", "look": []}]}, {"id": "1.2", "title": "Comparing and ordering", "objs": ["O2"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Bean count", "p": ["Class A grew **428** beans. Class B grew **482**.", "Which class grew more? How can you tell quickly? Think before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Bigger and smaller", "p": ["70 is bigger than 40."], "qq": {"id": "m3u01s2t01", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Bigger: 59 or 61?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "61", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "59", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Comparing", "p": ["Compare the **hundreds** first. If they are the same, compare the **tens**, then the **ones**.", "428 and 482: hundreds 4 = 4; tens **2 < 8** → **428 < 482**. Class B grew more."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Symbols", "p": [], "table": {"head": ["Symbol", "Meaning", "Example"], "rows": [["<", "is less than", "428 < 482"], [">", "is greater than", "615 > 561"], ["=", "is equal to", "300 + 4 = 304"]]}, "p2": ["The open side faces the bigger number."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Sign", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m3u01s2t02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "371 ☐ 317", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "<", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": ">", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "=", "ok": false, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I compare and order numbers?", "p": ["Step 1: Line up the digits.", "Step 2: Compare hundreds, then tens, then ones.", "Step 3: Use <, > or =.", "Step 4: To order, find the smallest, then the next…"]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Compare", "p": [], "q": "706 and 760.", "steps": [["tens: 0 < 6", ""]], "a": "706 < 760"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Order", "p": [], "q": "Order 251, 215, 521.", "steps": [["hundreds: 2, 2, 5", ""], ["tens: 5 vs 1", ""]], "a": "215, 251, 521"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Between", "p": [], "q": "A number between 390 and 400.", "steps": [["391 to 399", ""]], "a": "e.g. 395"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Equal", "p": [], "q": "500 + 30 ☐ 530.", "steps": [["both 530", ""]], "a": "="}, {"k": "try", "t": "Order", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m3u01s2t03", "type": "short", "prompt": "Order from smallest: 340, 304, 430. Separate them with commas.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "accept": ["304, 340, 430", "/^\\s*304\\s*[,; ]\\s*340\\s*[,; ]\\s*430\\s*$/"], "hint": "", "reason": "304, 340, 430."}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Comparing the ones first", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Compare 289 and 312.", "lines": ["9 > 2, so 289 > 312"], "bad": 0, "why": "Start with hundreds: 2 < 3, so 289 < 312.", "fix": [["289 < 312", ""]], "id": "m3u01s2t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Starting with the ones", "p": ["Always start with the biggest place – hundreds."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Comparing prices, scores and heights of buildings."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["Compare hundreds, tens, then ones.", "< less than, > greater than, = equal.", "Order smallest to largest or largest to smallest."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 660, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "1.2-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m3u01s2k01", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Before you read on: more beans?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "Class B (482)", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "Class A (428)", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"id": "1.2-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m3u01s2k02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "615 ☐ 561", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "<", "ok": false, "fb": ""}, {"t": ">", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "=", "ok": false, "fb": ""}], "fixed": true}}, {"id": "1.2-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m3u01s2k03", "type":